---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Logo from '../components/Logo.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="homerunn — Full-Stack Growth Marketing"
  description="Most ecommerce brands aren't short on marketing activity. They're short on content that builds a confident buyer. homerunn builds the full system. The sales follow."
>

  <!-- NAV -->
  <header class="fixed top-0 left-0 right-0 z-50 bg-white border-b border-[#E5E5E5]">
    <div class="max-w-[1100px] mx-auto px-6 h-16 flex items-center justify-between">
      <a href="/"><Logo color="amber" width={120} /></a>
      <a
        href="#contact"
        class="bg-[#D97706] hover:bg-[#B45309] text-white font-inter font-semibold text-sm px-5 py-2.5 rounded transition-colors"
      >
        Let's talk
      </a>
    </div>
  </header>

  <!-- HERO -->
  <section class="bg-[#111111] diamond-texture pt-40 pb-24 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto">
      <p class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-6">
        For ecommerce brands doing $100K–$3M in revenue
      </p>
      <h1 class="font-sora font-bold text-5xl md:text-6xl text-white leading-tight mb-6">
        The best marketing educates first. The sales follow.
      </h1>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-xl leading-relaxed mb-6 max-w-[620px]">
        Most ecommerce brands aren't short on marketing activity. They're short on content that builds a confident buyer. That gap is where revenue lives.
      </p>
      <!-- Proof bar -->
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-2 mb-10 font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-sm">
        <span><span class="text-[#D97706] font-semibold">575%</span> revenue growth</span>
        <span class="text-[#2A2A2A]">·</span>
        <span><span class="text-[#D97706] font-semibold">$453K</span> email revenue</span>
        <span class="text-[#2A2A2A]">·</span>
        <span><span class="text-[#D97706] font-semibold">40,000+</span> organic keywords</span>
        <span class="text-[#2A2A2A]">·</span>
        <span>Writing <span class="text-[#D97706] font-semibold">cited in Forbes</span></span>
      </div>
      <a
        href="#contact"
        class="inline-block bg-[#D97706] hover:bg-[#B45309] text-white font-inter font-semibold text-base px-8 py-4 rounded transition-colors"
      >
        Start the Conversation
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE PROBLEM -->
  <section class="bg-white py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto">
      <p class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">The problem</p>
      <h2 class="font-sora font-bold text-4xl text-[#111111] leading-tight mb-8">Why Good Products Don't Always Sell</h2>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
        The problem isn't the products. It's the marketing around them.
      </p>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Most content is built for buyers who already know what they want. It describes the products, lists the specs, shows the price. That works fine for capturing demand that already exists. It does nothing to build it.
      </p>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg leading-relaxed mb-10">
        The customers who come back, buy more, and bring others need something different. They need to understand their situation before they're asked to decide. They need to trust the brand before they're asked to buy. When the marketing skips that work, you get traffic, the occasional sale, and no real relationship.
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-3">
        {[
          "Content that describes the products but never builds trust in the brand",
          "Nothing that helps a buyer understand their situation or feel confident about the decision",
          "Email that exists but doesn't teach or earn revenue",
          "Traffic that bounces because the pages don't answer the real questions",
          "Ads driving clicks to a site that can't close",
        ].map((item) => (
          <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="text-[#D97706] font-bold mt-1">—</span>
            <span class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg">{item}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE FIX -->
  <section class="bg-[#111111] diamond-texture py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto">
      <p class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">The fix</p>
      <h2 class="font-sora font-bold text-4xl text-white leading-tight mb-8">Marketing Built Around the Confident Buyer. Everything Else Follows.</h2>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
        A confident buyer goes through four stages.
      </p>
      <div class="space-y-4 mb-6">
        <div>
          <span class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-lg">1. Their situation.</span>
          <span class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg"> What they're dealing with, why it matters, and how to think about the decision.</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-lg">2. The products.</span>
          <span class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg"> What they are, how they work, and why they're the right fit.</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-lg">3. The brand.</span>
          <span class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg"> The story, the point of view, the people behind it.</span>
        </div>
        <div>
          <span class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-lg">4. What buying from you is actually like.</span>
          <span class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg"> The process, what to expect, what happens after.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
        Most brands cover the products and stop there. The ones that build all four are the ones with conversion rates that make the math work: lower ad costs, higher AOV, fewer refunds, more repeat buyers.
      </p>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
        That's the system I build. SEO brings in buyers who already understand their situation. Email teaches and keeps people coming back. The pages behind ads answer every question before it's asked. The brand story makes you memorable instead of interchangeable.
      </p>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg leading-relaxed">
        I've been building this for a specialty ecommerce retailer for years and the business keeps growing. That's what I do at homerunn.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT YOU GET -->
  <section id="services" class="bg-[#F7F7F7] py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-[1100px] mx-auto">
      <div class="max-w-[760px] mb-16">
        <p class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">What you get</p>
        <h2 class="font-sora font-bold text-4xl text-[#111111] leading-tight">Full-Stack Growth Marketing. One Operator Running the System.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-8">
        {[
          {
            title: 'SEO & Organic Growth',
            body: 'Technical SEO, content strategy, keyword targeting. Not rankings for the sake of rankings. Traffic that actually converts.',
            proof: 'Grew organic keywords from 9,000 to 40,000+.',
          },
          {
            title: 'Email Marketing (Klaviyo)',
            body: "Full email programs built from zero. Flows, campaigns, segmentation, list growth. Email becomes a revenue channel, not a backlog item.",
            proof: 'Built a Klaviyo program from zero to $453K in attributed revenue. Top 10% of platform operators.',
          },
          {
            title: 'Content & CRO',
            body: 'Landing pages, product pages, blog content. Written to explain the products clearly, build trust, and turn visitors into buyers.',
            proof: '17% average order value increase through CRO and landing page optimization.',
          },
          {
            title: 'Website Development',
            body: "I lead the build and bring in a designer and developer to execute it. Brand story, page structure, product presentation. The website is the foundation everything else runs on.",
            proof: '',
          },
          {
            title: 'Meta Ads',
            body: 'Campaign strategy, creative direction, audience building, retargeting. Connected to the rest of the system so every dollar works harder.',
            proof: '',
          },
          {
            title: 'Strategy & Reporting',
            body: "Clear attribution and honest reporting. You know what's working, what's not, and what to do next. No dashboards full of vanity metrics.",
            proof: '',
          },
        ].map(({ title, body, proof }) => (
          <div class="bg-white border border-[#E5E5E5] rounded-lg p-8">
            <p class="font-sora font-semibold text-lg text-[#111111] mb-3">{title}</p>
            <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-base leading-relaxed mb-3">{body}</p>
            {proof && <p class="font-inter text-[#D97706] text-sm font-semibold">{proof}</p>}
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE NUMBERS -->
  <section class="bg-[#111111] diamond-texture py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-[1100px] mx-auto">
      <div class="max-w-[760px] mb-16">
        <p class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">The numbers</p>
        <h2 class="font-sora font-bold text-4xl text-white leading-tight mb-4">Results I Can Show You</h2>
        <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg leading-relaxed">
          The average ecommerce brand grows around 8–9% a year. What you see below came from running every channel for a specialty ecommerce retailer — work I'm still doing today. The growth is in the method. It doesn't hurt to work with a brand that actually delivers on its promise and treats people right.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-3 gap-px bg-[#1F1F1F]">
        {[
          { stat: '$2.7M', label: 'Annual revenue, up from $400K (575% growth)' },
          { stat: '$300K+', label: 'Single-month revenue milestone' },
          { stat: '$453K', label: 'Email attributed revenue via Klaviyo' },
          { stat: '40,000+', label: 'Organic keywords ranked (up from 9,000)' },
          { stat: '17%', label: 'AOV increase through CRO' },
          { stat: 'Forbes', label: 'Writing cited in a Forbes.com article (200K+ views)' },
        ].map(({ stat, label }) => (
          <div class="bg-[#111111] p-8">
            <p class="font-sora font-bold text-4xl text-[#D97706] mb-2">{stat}</p>
            <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-sm leading-snug">{label}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-sm mt-6 max-w-[620px]">
        The paid ads that drive much of the site's revenue convert because of the brand story, landing pages, and product experience built alongside them. The system is the asset.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHO THIS IS FOR -->
  <section class="bg-white py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto">
      <p class="font-inter text-[#111111] text-lg leading-relaxed mb-16">
        The brands I work with are building something real. They have a product people actually want, a story worth telling, and usually a founder who knows their customer better than any agency ever will. They just need the marketing to catch up. That's the work I'm here for.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12">
      <div>
        <p class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-6">This is for you if...</p>
        <ul class="space-y-4">
          {[
            'You run an ecommerce brand doing $100K–$3M and marketing is holding you back',
            "You've tried specialists or agencies and nothing connected",
            'You want one person to own the system and make sure everything works together',
            'Your email is underperforming or abandoned entirely',
            "You know you're leaving money on the table but can't pinpoint where",
          ].map((item) => (
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-[#D97706] font-bold mt-0.5">✓</span>
              <span class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-base leading-relaxed">{item}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-6">This probably isn't for you if...</p>
        <ul class="space-y-4">
          {[
            "You need someone to manage a team of marketers (I'm the operator, not the manager)",
            "You're looking for a pure Google PPC specialist (I can connect you with one)",
            "You're looking for the cheapest option",
            "You need results in 30 days (this work compounds over months)",
          ].map((item) => (
            <li class="flex items-start gap-3">
              <span class="text-[#6B7280] font-bold mt-0.5">×</span>
              <span class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-base leading-relaxed">{item}</span>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="bg-[#F7F7F7] py-28 px-6 border-t border-[#E5E5E5]">
    <div class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto">
      <p class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">Common questions</p>
      <h2 class="font-sora font-bold text-4xl text-[#111111] leading-tight mb-12">Probably wondering...</h2>
      <div class="space-y-10">
        {[
          {
            q: 'Can one person really handle all of this?',
            a: "Yes. I run the system and own every channel: SEO, email, content, Meta ads, CRO. When a project needs it, I bring in people who are genuinely good at what they do — a designer and developer, a writer, a PPC specialist, and someone I work closely with on growth tactics. You still get one person who owns the strategy and makes sure everything connects.",
          },
          {
            q: 'How do I know your results will transfer to my business?',
            a: "They're proof of a process, not a single lucky outcome. Connected channels that compound work across ecommerce verticals. I'd rather show you than tell you. A defined project is a good way to see the approach before committing to anything ongoing.",
          },
          {
            q: 'What does this cost?',
            a: "Depends on scope. Retainers are for businesses that want full-stack marketing run on an ongoing basis. Project work is for a specific deliverable: email setup, SEO audit, content strategy, site build. Either way, it costs less than an agency and less than a full-time hire. We'll talk numbers once I understand your situation.",
          },
          {
            q: 'What if I just need help with one channel?',
            a: "Start there. Project work is a real option and a low-commitment way to see how I work. Fair warning: once you see what happens when channels actually connect, the single-channel thinking tends to go away.",
          },
          {
            q: 'Are you just using AI to do the work?',
            a: "AI is part of how I work. I used to write everything myself — every email, every article, every ad. Now AI drafts faster, but the strategy, the judgment, and the final call are still mine. The results you're looking at came from years before any of these tools existed.",
          },
          {
            q: 'Do you work with local businesses too?',
            a: "Yes. That's where I started. Websites and digital marketing for local service businesses and specialty retailers. If you want to grow online or sell nationally, that experience is directly relevant. Worth a conversation.",
          },
        ].map(({ q, a }) => (
          <div class="border-b border-[#E5E5E5] pb-10">
            <p class="font-sora font-semibold text-xl text-[#111111] mb-3">{q}</p>
            <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-base leading-relaxed">{a}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- HOW TO START -->
  <section class="bg-white py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto">
      <p class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">How to start</p>
      <h2 class="font-sora font-bold text-4xl text-[#111111] leading-tight mb-12">Here's How This Works</h2>
      <div class="space-y-8">
        {[
          { step: '01', text: 'Fill out the form below. Tell me about your business and where you\'re stuck.' },
          { step: '02', text: "I'll review it and get back to you within 48 hours." },
          { step: '03', text: "We get on a call. I'll ask questions, look at your setup, and tell you exactly what I'd do first." },
          { step: '04', text: "We pick a starting point. Retainer or project. Whatever makes sense for where you are." },
        ].map(({ step, text }) => (
          <div class="flex items-start gap-6">
            <span class="font-sora font-bold text-3xl text-[#D97706] w-12 shrink-0">{step}</span>
            <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg leading-relaxed pt-1">{text}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-base mt-10 italic">No slideshow. No pressure. Just a conversation about your marketing.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ABOUT -->
  <section id="about" class="bg-[#F7F7F7] py-28 px-6 border-t border-[#E5E5E5]">
    <div class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto">
      <p class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">About</p>
      <h2 class="font-sora font-bold text-4xl text-[#111111] leading-tight mb-8">Who's Behind This</h2>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
        I'm Marc St. John, a marketer and writer based in Columbus, Ohio.
      </p>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
        For the past four years I've led the marketing for a specialty ecommerce retailer — SEO and content strategy, landing page optimization, and website development alongside a designer and developer. In the last year I added Klaviyo email and Meta ads. Both moved fast: email hit $453K in attributed revenue and I'm in the top 10% of Klaviyo operators. Every channel running together. The business went from $400K to $2.7M. I'm also a former English teacher. It turns out that's better preparation for this work than most marketing degrees.
      </p>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg leading-relaxed mb-8">
        The other thing that shaped how I work: I spent my whole life playing baseball. Hitting, specifically. High pressure, public, and the feedback is immediate. You barrel it or you don't. What it taught me is to refine the approach, trust the work, and let the numbers tell the truth. Marketing works the same way.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CONTACT -->
  <section id="contact" class="bg-[#111111] diamond-texture py-28 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-[760px] mx-auto">
      <p class="font-inter text-[#D97706] font-semibold text-sm uppercase tracking-widest mb-4">Get in touch</p>
      <h2 class="font-sora font-bold text-4xl text-white leading-tight mb-4">
        Ready to build marketing that earns the sale before it asks for one?
      </h2>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-lg leading-relaxed mb-12">
        Fill out the form. Tell me where you are and what's not moving. I'll get back to you within 48 hours and tell you honestly if I can help.
      </p>
      <form name="contact" method="POST" data-netlify="true" class="space-y-5">
        <input type="hidden" name="form-name" value="contact" />
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
          <div>
            <label for="name" class="block font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-sm mb-2">Your name</label>
            <input id="name" name="name" type="text" required
              class="w-full bg-[#1A1A1A] border border-[#2A2A2A] text-white font-inter text-base px-4 py-3 rounded focus:outline-none focus:border-[#D97706] transition-colors"
              placeholder="Jane Smith" />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="business" class="block font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-sm mb-2">Business name</label>
            <input id="business" name="business" type="text"
              class="w-full bg-[#1A1A1A] border border-[#2A2A2A] text-white font-inter text-base px-4 py-3 rounded focus:outline-none focus:border-[#D97706] transition-colors"
              placeholder="Your Brand" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-5">
          <div>
            <label for="website" class="block font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-sm mb-2">Website URL</label>
            <input id="website" name="website" type="text"
              class="w-full bg-[#1A1A1A] border border-[#2A2A2A] text-white font-inter text-base px-4 py-3 rounded focus:outline-none focus:border-[#D97706] transition-colors"
              placeholder="https://yourbrand.com" />
          </div>
          <div>
            <label for="email" class="block font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-sm mb-2">Email address</label>
            <input id="email" name="email" type="email" required
              class="w-full bg-[#1A1A1A] border border-[#2A2A2A] text-white font-inter text-base px-4 py-3 rounded focus:outline-none focus:border-[#D97706] transition-colors"
              placeholder="your@email.com" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <label for="message" class="block font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-sm mb-2">What's your biggest marketing challenge right now?</label>
          <textarea id="message" name="message" rows="5" required
            class="w-full bg-[#1A1A1A] border border-[#2A2A2A] text-white font-inter text-base px-4 py-3 rounded focus:outline-none focus:border-[#D97706] transition-colors resize-none"
            placeholder="Tell me where you are. Revenue, channels you're running, what's not moving..."></textarea>
        </div>
        <button type="submit"
          class="bg-[#D97706] hover:bg-[#B45309] text-white font-inter font-semibold text-base px-8 py-4 rounded transition-colors">
          Let's Talk
        </button>
      </form>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FOOTER -->
  <footer class="bg-[#111111] border-t border-[#1F1F1F] py-8 px-6">
    <div class="max-w-[1100px] mx-auto flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4">
      <a href="/"><Logo color="amber" width={100} /></a>
      <p class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] text-sm">&copy; {new Date().getFullYear()} homerunn. Columbus, OH.</p>
      <a href="/blog" class="font-inter text-[#6B7280] hover:text-white text-sm transition-colors">Blog</a>
    </div>
  </footer>

</Layout>
